# J27 — Local monorepo baseline: scan plan, Run Focus, cancellation receipt.
#
# Against the real local monorepo checkout, captures (1) the guided Map-to-Scan workflow
# plan surfaces (route + module cards) without launching a scan, then
# (2) a live Run Focus over a deterministic runtime-free run
# (`context:build`), an operator cancellation, and whatever receipt the
# cancellation actually produces. The contract requires canceled work to
# land as an honest canceled/partial receipt that earns no coverage
# credit; whatever the product does today is recorded as baseline truth.
#
# Never deletes pre-existing `.kuzushi` engagement state; never touches
# target sources or git state.
name: Monorepo baseline · scan plan and cancellation receipt
require-env: KUZUSHI_DEVEX_TARGET
size: 120x36
env-unset: ANTHROPIC_API_KEY OPENAI_API_KEY NO_COLOR
env: HOME=@TMP_HOME COLORTERM=truecolor KUZUSHI_REDUCED_MOTION=1 KUZUSHI_SKIP_ONBOARDING=1
launch: --target @TARGET
wait-for: 60 KUZUSHI
submit: /full
wait-for: 20 MAP · ROUTE
snap: scan-route
ask: Route — is the guided route derived from the real target state (context/coverage present or missing), and does it lead root-first when no holistic baseline exists?
keys: Enter
wait-for: 15 MAP · MODULES
snap: scan-modules
ask: Modules — are module recommendations tied to recorded evidence from this checkout, with honest disclosure when the recommender has nothing real to stand on?
keys: Escape
wait: 1
keys: Escape
wait: 1
submit: run context:build {}
wait-live-snap: 60 RUN FOCUS | run-focus-live
ask: Run Focus — do task identities and output lines reflect the real whole-repo build (real paths/counts), with honest liveness signals at this repository scale?
keys: C-c
wait: 2
snap: cancel-requested
wait-for: 180 canceled
wait: 2
snap: cancel-receipt
ask: Cancellation — does the canceled run land as an honest canceled/partial receipt (no completion claim, no coverage credit), with a clear return path to the Map page?
nav-mode:
keys: 1
wait-live-snap: 30 Viewing Map | map-after-cancel
ask: Map after cancel — does the page reflect the canceled attempt truthfully (no forged progress), and is the dominant NEXT still the root-first action?
keys: Escape
